course: dictionary
lesson: 5600
title: Lieutenant: an officer or a helper
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A lieutenant is an officer in the army, navy or air force, of junior to middle rank. «The lieutenant led a small group of soldiers across the muddy field.» The word tells you the lieutenant is in charge of a few soldiers, not the whole army, so it is not a top rank.
explain: The word can also mean a helper. «The boss's lieutenant ran the shop while the boss was away.» The clue is that the boss was away, so someone had to act for him. A lieutenant here is a deputy, a person who helps and acts for the leader.
explain: «After 1066 many English words for law, the army and cooking came from French, like "jury", "lieutenant" and "chef".» The words around lieutenant are law, army and cooking, and they tell you the word belongs to the army and to leadership. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then check your meaning in the sentence.
fact: A lieutenant is an officer in the army, navy or air force, of junior to middle rank.
fact: A lieutenant can also be a deputy: a person who helps and acts for a leader.
fact: In the United States, a lieutenant can be a police or fire officer of middle rank.
fact: «Lieutenant» came into English from French after 1066, just like «chef» and «jury».
fact: Lt is the short form (abbreviation) of lieutenant.
exercise: «The lieutenant led a small group of soldiers across the field.» What is a lieutenant? | A kind of horse ridden in battles | A cook who prepares food for the army | *An officer in the army, navy or air force | A soldier with no rank at all
exercise: «The boss's lieutenant ran the shop while the boss was away.» What does lieutenant mean here? | A rival boss from another town | *A deputy who helps and acts for the leader | A customer who visits the shop each day | A stranger who buys the shop
exercise: Copy the word from «After 1066 many English words for law, the army and cooking came from French, like "jury", "lieutenant" and "chef".» that is a word for cooking. | army | French | law | *chef
test: What does the short form Lt stand for? | Loft | Lottery | Leader | *Lieutenant
test: In the United States, a lieutenant can be a police or fire officer. Is this true? | *True | Only in the navy | False | Only in old history books
exam: After 1066, which language gave English the word lieutenant? | Latin | Scots | *French | German
